4. Syracuse step S(n) = (3n+1)/2^v for odd n: exponent move (-v,+1)
   v=1: bishop (1,1)   density 1/2 (exact 2^-v = 1/2)
   v=2: knight (1,2)   density 1/4 (exact 2^-v = 1/4)
   v=3: camel (1,3)    density 1/8 (exact 2^-v = 1/8)
   v=4: giraffe (1,4)  density 1/16 (exact 2^-v = 1/16)
   v=5: (1,5)-leaper   density 1/32 (exact 2^-v = 1/32)
   v=6: (1,6)-leaper   density 1/64 (exact 2^-v = 1/64)
   mean leap = (-E v, +1) = (-2, +1) = the knight; log-drift per odd step = log(3/4) = -0.2876820724517809
   critical slope log2 3 = 1.584962500721156 lies strictly between bishop (1) and knight (2)

5. 3n+1 maps every odd n to an even number (colour switch): checked n < 1e5
   k= 1: density of odd n (mod 2^4) with k bishop/knight leaps = 3/4 (3/4)^k = 3/4
   k= 2: density of odd n (mod 2^6) with k bishop/knight leaps = 9/16 (3/4)^k = 9/16
   k= 4: density of odd n (mod 2^10) with k bishop/knight leaps = 81/256 (3/4)^k = 81/256
   k= 8: density of odd n (mod 2^18) with k bishop/knight leaps = 6561/65536 (3/4)^k = 6561/65536
   k=12: density of odd n (mod 2^26) with k bishop/knight leaps = 531441/16777216 (3/4)^k = 531441/16777216
